## Context

Tracker 0406, final step S5. The phase .mks exist (acquire.mk, score.mk,
render.mk, report/ and slides/ Makefiles). The root Makefile still
carries cross-phase machinery: a `$(MEASUREMENTS)` wildcard rule
delegating to score.mk, long P3 prereq lists on `report/report.pdf` and
`slides/slides.pdf`, and delegating aliases (tables, figures, census,
select, measurements). S5 rewrites root to the ratified shape.

## Ratified design (tracker 0406)

Root = dev loop (test/test-fast/test-slow/coverage/lint/check-fast/
check, show-prompts) + the full pipeline DAG exposed through EXACTLY
TWO cross-phase entries:

- `make staleness` — dry-run report: what would rebuild across P2+P3
  (+P4), touches nothing.
- `make world` — deliberate full re-run of P2+P3+P4; output reviewed
  via `git diff` before committing (this is ticket 0360's CI oracle:
  `make world && git diff --exit-code`).

Constraints:
- `make report`, `make slides`, `make check` keep working for CI
  (docs-build.yml) — but as PURE P4 verbs: `report:` and `slides:`
  delegate to `$(MAKE) -C report` / `-C slides` with NO generated-file
  prerequisite lists (the writing build consumes committed artifacts;
  clean-room tests already guard this). DELETE the P3 prereq lists and
  the `report/report.pdf` / `slides/slides.pdf` wrapper rules' prereqs.
- No other root target may carry a cross-phase prerequisite edge.
  Remove: the `$(MEASUREMENTS)` wildcard rule + `measurements` verb,
  `tables`, `figures`, `select`, `census` aliases (per-phase .mks are
  the documented dev path; README documents the invocations).
  `experiments/models_selected.yaml` rule: relocate to acquire.mk
  (it configures sweeps) or drop to README documentation — decide and
  flag.
- **P1 is excluded from world/staleness** (money gate — a full re-run
  must never trigger API sweeps). Document this exclusion in the root
  header and docs/pipeline-phases.md.

## Mechanism guidance (binding intent, flexible mechanism)

The tracker text says "include of all phase .mks". HAZARDS found
during S2-S4 that the implementer must reconcile:
- acquire.mk recipes assume cwd=experiments/ (env contract ../.env,
  experiments.toml, jobs/). It is P1 → NOT included (excluded above).
- score.mk captures its self-path via $(lastword $(MAKEFILE_LIST))
  BEFORE its includes and recurses via that absolute path — verify
  this survives being `include`d by root (MAKEFILE_LIST differs), and
  that paths.mk/common.mk double-inclusion (root → score.mk AND
  render.mk both include them) is idempotent (?=, no rule dups).
- If literal `include` proves unsound, the fallback preserving the
  ratified INTENT (one visible full DAG behind two entries) is
  recursive delegation: `world: ; $(MAKE) -f experiments/derived/score.mk all-outcomes
  && $(MAKE) -f experiments/render.mk all && $(MAKE) -C report && $(MAKE) -C slides`
  and `staleness:` as the same chain with -n + a one-line-per-target
  summary. Choose whichever is sound, document the choice in the PR
  body and the root header comment.
- `world` runs P2 for REAL — that rewrites committed scored data
  (0383). That is its PURPOSE (deliberate, reviewed via git diff), but
  the implementer must NOT run `make world` during development of this
  PR beyond `-n` verification. Add a prominent recipe comment: output
  must be reviewed via git diff before commit. If a cheap guard is
  feasible (e.g. refuse to run with a dirty working tree), add it.

